<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  DAR-BE-318 plan 3b-1 (ruling P3b1-9). What the NetSuite endpoints do that darpan core must know without naming NetSuite: set
  here, on the core connector row by primary key (the other fields stay core's), never in core.

  excludedRecordsSidecar Y: the records Keep sets aside are written beside the extract (the side file). Since DAR-BE-318
  plan 3b-2b the extract filters nothing and Spark writes that file (ruling 3b2b-3); a kept-copy slice writes it when this says Y.

  keepLinesJson (ruling 3b2b-12): NetSuite's built-in Keep line, run in Spark before the tenant's own filters. A SALES_LINES
    line with no HotWax line id (a store-credit payment line) is written with nsUnkeyedLine "Y"; this line sets it aside, and
    its side-file entry reads _excludedBy "0:orderLineId", as the extractor wrote it before. Never counted as a tenant
    exclusion. Upgrade-pack row: this value on the NETSUITE_SUITEQL row.

  datasetReadParametersJson {"datasetRead":true}: sent on every dataset read of the endpoint (Task 5). The read stamps each
    record with darpanStamp (the later of its header lastmodifieddate and newest line's linelastmodifieddate), ends a full
    read on the dateColumn the day after the one sent so today is in it, and refuses any template but RECORDS and SALES_LINES,
    so a dataset on one fails its first read and never builds a copy (ruling P3b1-14). A run read sends none of it.
    A NetSuite dataset is stored with windowField = the query's dateColumn (e.g. trandate, not the record field it maps to)
    and stampField = darpanStamp. Its idField must name one record: for RECORDS a transaction key (e.g. netsuiteInternalId);
    for SALES_LINES a header key plus lineId (e.g. tranId,lineId), because lineId is transactionline.id, a line number within
    its own order (line 1 of every order shares it). Keyed by lineId alone a read fails (ruling P3b1-15).

  servingProjectionServiceName: project#NetSuiteKeptRecords refuses every side, so a NetSuite run reads live (ruling P3b1-6):
    served parity is not proven on the real record shape. The row names no windowFieldName either; this keeps a copy from
    being served even if it is given one. See NetSuiteKeptCopyTests.
-->
<entity-facade-xml type="darpan-seed">
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector systemEnumId="NETSUITE_SUITEQL" excludedRecordsSidecar="Y"
            servingProjectionServiceName="reconciliation.NetSuiteOrderExtractionServices.project#NetSuiteKeptRecords"
            datasetReadParametersJson='{"datasetRead":true}'
            keepLinesJson='[{"sequenceNum":0,"label":"orderLineId","kinds":{"nsUnkeyedLine":"FVT_TEXT"},"lines":[{"conditionSeqId":"01","conditionTypeId":"RCT_COMPARE","fieldName":"nsUnkeyedLine","operatorEnumId":"ENTCO_EQUALS","compareValue":"Y"}]}]'/>
</entity-facade-xml>
